      "writtenOn": "2023-05-31T11:10:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How does other Android components test code involving handlers ?\n\nI really don\u0027t like all those syncHandler, if possible I would prefer that we make the Handler sync itself.\n\nIt seems that Roboelectric has a method to wait for a looper to be idle which is close to this syncHandler :/ https://robolectric.org/blog/2019/06/04/paused-looper/.\n\nI also found https://medium.com/@kcoppock/mocking-an-android-handler-to-immediately-invoke-a-runnable-58bf09bb1eba that give a hack to make the Handler synchronous.\n\nI wonder also if we could not avoid all those sync handlers by running the test itself on the Handler (so that they have the same Looper)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 297,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 297,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "71d57d69da4226c3d29ce612e22e58ff436b33f9",
